WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.270
In this lesson, you will learn to build a numeric model that changes over time, and an agent-based model where many clones follow simple rules.

2
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:18.887
A model keeps the important parts of reality and ignores the rest.

3
00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:23.600
Scientists use models to predict weather, diseases and populations.

4
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:31.087
Many models update in time steps: each “year”, the population changes by a rule.

5
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:34.061
A loop runs the years.

6
00:00:34.661 --> 00:00:37.635
Real populations can’t grow forever.

7
00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:43.217
Add a capacity: if pop > 500, set pop to 500.

8
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:46.626
Better models add more realistic rules.

9
00:00:47.226 --> 00:00:54.548
Instead of one number, simulate many individuals (agents) — each a clone following simple rules.

10
00:00:54.548 --> 00:00:57.957
Interesting patterns emerge from the crowd.

11
00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:08.052
The same model in Python: a loop for the years, a rule for growth and a rule for the limit.

12
00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:12.496
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

13
00:01:12.496 --> 00:01:17.643
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
